        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-798",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Hard-coded AWS secret access key in settings.py.\n\nAWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY is a literal string in source.\n\nImpact: Anyone with repository or artifact access holds live cloud credentials.\n\nExploit scenario: Clone the repo, export the two variables, call the AWS API as the application identity.\n\nPreconditions: Repository read access.\n\nRecommendation: Rotate the key; load credentials from the environment or a secrets manager.\n\nThe source line is not quoted because it holds the credential.\n\nCWE-798. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
